  :authoritative_for
  ["honest record of an OPEN, UNRESOLVED defect in kotoba.sm.gtg's Phase 1
    field-equation pipeline (omega-from-h/riemann-map/riemann-basis-pair/
    curvature-scalar) -- not a fix. Documented prominently in code (PR #14,
    docstring-only, no behavior change) rather than left as a latent trap"
   "BUG: curvature-scalar returns EXACTLY 7x the correct value for any h-field
    with genuinely time-varying expansion rate (Hdot!=0) -- e.g. Einstein-de
    Sitter matter-dominated dust, H(t)=2/(3t). Independently reproduced by 2
    people (investigating agent + requester in a fresh REPL), ratio stable at
    7.00000000 (7-8 sig figs) across fd-h in [5e-5,1e-3] and t in [1.5,10] --
    a clean algebraic sign error, not FD truncation noise"
   "correct answer independently confirmed GTG-FREE: ordinary Christoffel-symbol
    computation on the metric this h-bar represents gives R=-12*H^2-6*Hdot
    (standard FRW textbook result); this pipeline computes -12*H^2+6*Hdot --
    ONLY the Hdot (time-derivative) term has wrong sign, H^2 term is exactly
    correct"
   "why undetected by 2 prior independent reviews: BOTH existing regression
    solutions (Schwarzschild=static, de Sitter=constant H) have Hdot=0
    identically, structurally cannot exercise the time-derivative channel.
    FOURTH instance of silently-wrong-result-surviving-review in this repo's
    GTG work (after PR #6 slot order, Phase 1 first-attempt wrong covariant
    derivative, PR #11 double-h bug) -- first that 2 independent multi-hour
    investigations could NOT resolve to a confident root cause"
   "what was checked and found individually correct in isolation: H-field
    (symbolic general H(t), structurally zero Hdot-dependence by construction),
    omega-from-h (checked against eq 4.50 directly + independent Python GA
    engine, exact match), L-a-omega (eq 4.42 identity a.hbar(grad)F=h(a).grad F
    verified on a PLAIN SCALAR test function F(x)=t,a=e_0, no bivector/GA
    machinery -- exact match; commutator eq 4.44 also checked directly,
    matched to 1e-13), riemann-basis-pair (eq 4.44->4.46->4.47->4.48 chain
    re-derived by hand, line-by-line match). YET end-to-end composition is
    measurably wrong specifically in the time-derivative channel. Symbolic
    isolation: code computes R(e0^e1)=-H^2+H', correct tetrad value is
    -H^2-H'"
   "declined patch: negating L-a-omega's rho=0 (time-direction) contribution
    only numerically fixes the dust case and provably doesn't affect
    Schwarzschild/de-Sitter (both structurally zero rho=0 contribution) --
    but DELIBERATELY NOT APPLIED because it contradicts the simpler,
    independent scalar-function identity check (a.hbar(grad)F=h(a).grad F on
    F(x)=t) -- applying the patch would make THAT more fundamental check
    fail. Symptom suppression, not a verified fix; would reintroduce exactly
    the tests-pass-code-is-wrong failure mode this investigative lineage
    exists to prevent"
   "decision: do not land any fix without confident independently-verified
    root cause. Document prominently instead (CONFIRMED UNRESOLVED BUG notice
    in namespace docstring PHASE 1 SCOPE NOTE + curvature-scalar's own
    docstring): Schwarzschild (static) and de Sitter (Hdot=0) remain verified
    and safe; any h-field with Hdot!=0 is NOT safe to trust through this
    pipeline until resolved. No new test added for dust case (would either
    fail, or misleadingly signal resolved). No existing test/code modified --
    79 tests/2911 assertions unchanged"
   "recommended next steps for future work: (1) GTG/geometric-algebra domain
    expert consultation beyond what iterative independent re-derivation from
    the primary paper alone achieved; (2) cross-check against a THIRD
    independent exact time-dependent solution from literature (PDF page
    images, not pdftotext); (3) consider whether bug is not in any single
    named function but in an INTERACTION between H-field's INNER finite
    difference (differentiating hbar^-1) and L-a-omega's OUTER finite
    difference (differentiating omega-from-h itself) when both differentiate
    along the SAME coordinate (t) -- a 'finite difference of a finite
    difference' structure unique to this pipeline neither investigation
    fully ruled out"
   "methodological consequence extending ADR-2607103000: fourth instance of
    silently-wrong-invisible-to-tests failure mode, first that resisted 2
    genuine independent resolution attempts. Response is NOT to force a fix,
    guess-and-check against the one failing test, or lower the verification
    bar -- document honestly, decline the unverified patch, leave the defect
    visible. Future GTG regression solutions should be maximally DIFFERENT IN
    KIND from what's covered (a genuinely time-VARYING rate, not just
    'another named solution' -- de Sitter's own limitation despite being
    literally time-dependent in its metric, Hdot=0 made it insufficient,
    teaches this lesson)"]
